  "verbalization": "Didanosine, a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared biological pathway involving nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors. The evidence suggests that Didanosine, as part of this class of compounds, binds to Slc22a6, which is a transporter involved in the uptake of nucleosides. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which highlight the indirect connection between Didanosine and Slc22a6 through Stavudine or Zidovudine, both of which are also nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors. The lowest common ancestor of Didanosine and these compounds is the organic heteromonocyclic compound, reinforcing the structural and functional link. The mechanism appears to involve the interaction of nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors with Slc22a6, likely through their shared role in transporting nucleosides across cellular membranes. The evidence is consistent across different paths, suggesting a robust biological relationship that is supported by multiple layers of evidence.",
